{"id":"000VCP","title":"Feeding Friendsy: One Tough Cookie","author":"blackjackfitz","solvedCount":107,"difficulty":5,"rating":"96 %","firstSeen":"2026-10-17T17:33:19+00:00","posted":"am 13. Oktober 2026, 22:47 Uhr","rules":"At the time I was asked to contribute to this pack I wasn't setting much. Life with a newborn was really dominating my time. But I couldn't pass up the opportunity to make a somedoku for Marty's birthday. I knew immediately that I wanted to pay homage to one of my favorite somedokus, Some Kind of Chaos. by Marty Sears. I hope I did it justice.\n\nMy deep gratitude to VikingPrime for both organizing this pack and for doing the graphics of this puzzle. I have, reluctantly, modified the original artwork in order to make this more accessible to the largest possible audience. But, if you would like, you can still play this puzzle with the original design.\n\nRules\n\nFill the grid with the digits 1-9... there's more to it but we'll get there.\n\n#FRIENDSHIPGOALS\n\nIf you give blackcatfitz a cookie... he's going to ask for some milk! Help him reach the milk by finding a path through the maze of sweet treats. The path must not visit any cell more than once, cross itself or pass through any thick caramel walls.\n\nAs well as moving orthogonally, blackcatfitz may move diagonally — if there's a 2x2 space in which to do so — but may never pass diagonally through the rounded end / corner of a wall.\n\nSOMEDOKU\n\nFill every row 'n' and column 'n' with exactly 'n' different digits, chosen from the digits 1-9, repeating as necessary.\n\nCHAOS CONSTRUCTION\n\nDivide the grid into nine (9) regions, each containing nine (9) orthogonally connected cells. Given caramel walls always separate two different regions; however, any isolated, rounded wall pillars may exist wholly within one region.\n\nCOOKIES\n\nThe digit in a cookie indicates how many different digits appear in its region. For example, a digit 6 in a cookie indicates that the region includes 6 distinct digits (and therefore 3 repeats). No two cookies contain the same digit.\n\nDARK CHOCOLATE CHIPS\n\nCells sharing a dark chocolate chip must belong to the SAME region. Digits separated by a dark chocolate chip have a 1:2 ratio (one is double the other). Not all dark chocolate chips are given.\n\nWHITE CHOCOLATE CHIPS\n\nCells sharing a white chocolate chip must belong to DIFFERENT regions. Digits separated by a white chocolate chip are consecutive. Not all white chocolate chips are given.\n\nCRANBERRIES\n\nNote that blackcatfitz is allergic to cranberries — you must not include them on his path! If a cranberry sits between two digits one will be even and one will be odd. Not all cranberries have been given.\n\nTRIALS AND TRAILS\n\nIn this test of friendship, blackcatfitz must retrieve each of the nine cookies in numerical order (from 1-9) before returning to enjoy the milk. Good luck!","solutionCode":"Column 5 top to bottom","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/9y17z0wugq","kind":"sudokupad"},{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/pn630t41aj","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/9y17z0wugq","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-17T17:33:19+00:00"}